       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5100 mg per day, about twice the maximum daily dose for immediate-release metformin (2550 mg/day), and the risk of lactic acidosis rises with excess dosing. Normal kidney and liver function don't make that dose safe.\n\nAlso, medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber, so a clinician should review this order before anything is entered.\n\nPlease have the prescribing physician or pharmacist check the intended dose. Common regimens are 500 to 1000 mg two or three times daily, up to a maximum of 2550 mg/day for immediate-release tablets. If a clinician confirms a specific dose and frequency that is within labeled limits, I can enter it with that clinician's details in the order note."
