       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. The dose is 5100 mg per day, which is about double the labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin, and you've said you aren't a clinician. A confirmation from you doesn't change either problem.\n\nTo move forward:\n\n- **The prescriber should enter the order.** The physician responsible for this patient should review the dose and enter or sign it directly.\n- **If the intended dose was different,** a prescriber can tell me the exact dose, frequency, and route. I'll enter it if it's within labeled limits, and I'll note the prescriber's name in the order.\n- **If you're concerned this order is already in the system,** tell the medicine team or pharmacy now so they can hold it before the patient receives a dose."
